This file is the placeholder frontend/embed.go depends on.

`//go:embed all:dist` fails the build outright when dist/ holds no files, so
without something committed here neither `go build ./...` nor
`go test ./internal/...` works on a clone that has never run npm — and
internal/app imports this package, so that is most of the test suite.

Keeping this one file here means the binary compiles and serves an empty asset
tree instead: a broken UI, but a correct build, which is what lets the engine
be tested with no Node toolchain present. frontend.Built() reports false when
index.html is absent, and the app says so at startup rather than opening a
blank window.

`npm run build` fills this directory; .gitignore ignores everything in it
except this file.
